@Asaurus1 no a sleep, nor a loop with mini sleeps, nor a busy loop replicate this issue. 

I understand that the set of modules will not be changing, but my point was that this check itself will take some time, it must copy 2000 strings to a new set and then loop over those 2000 items and verify they are in the other set.

This is not a lot of work, however something like this could delay the sending of forward messages by just enough to cause the other thread to send its first message before the messages are sent.

Closing this since dynamically changing the value via the `value` parameter will not be supported. As discussed above, its just an initial value. It sometimes appears to work since changing the value parameter recreates the frontend widget. We are working on fixing this whenever `key` is set -> which would make this more reliable / less confusing: https://github.com/streamlit/streamlit/issues/11277

The way to dynamically change widget state values is via `key` and `st.session_state`, e.g.:

```python
import streamlit as st

topics_big = ["a", "b"]

if st.button("Select All"):
    for t in topics_big:
        st.session_state[f"topics_gigaselect_opinion_{t}"] = True
if st.button("Deselect All"):
    for t in topics_big:
        st.session_state[f"topics_gigaselect_opinion_{t}"] = False

for t in topics_big:
    st.checkbox(t, value=False, key=f"topics_gigaselect_opinion_{t}")
```
